Author: CusDeb OS Team
Description: explorer: show host window icons on external taskbar buttons.
 External task buttons had their icon hardcoded to NULL, so every button
 fell back to the generic OIC_SAMPLE glyph. The taskbar bridge now exports
 each window's _NET_WM_ICON to a content-hashed .ico file and advertises
 it in the state JSON. Parse the new "icon" field, cache the HICON per
 task item, reload it when the hashed path changes and retry on transient
 load failures (the bridge may rewrite the file a poll later). LoadImage
 is used instead of ExtractIconEx because the shell32 icon cache
 downscales the large icon instead of returning the real small one.
 The taskbar image list stays at the upstream ILC_COLOR32: the comctl32
 alpha-blending issue that once forced ILC_COLOR24 does not reproduce on
 Wine 11, and 32-bit lists render alpha icons with proper antialiased
 edges.
